        "original_id": "5c79ee3e-d051-57a3-9962-db050e925456",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Orange County Choppers, Orange County Ironworks\n- People: Paul Teutul Sr., Paul Teutul Jr.\n- Products/Brands: American Chopper\n- Places: Newburgh, Orange County, New York\n- Topics: motorcycle manufacturing, reality television\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Michael Teutul was born on October 2, 1974.\n- Before starring on American Chopper, Paul Teutul Jr. was head of the rail shop at Orange County Ironworks.\n- Orange County Choppers is a motorcycle manufacturer and lifestyle brand company based in Newburgh in Orange County, New York.\n- Orange County Choppers was founded in 1999 by Paul Teutul Sr. and Paul Teutul Jr.\n- American Chopper debuted on the Discovery Channel in September 2002 and featured Orange County Choppers.\n- Paul Teutul Jr. was one of the stars of the American reality television series American Chopper.\n- In 2007, American Chopper moved from Discovery Channel to its sister channel TLC.",
